+## Open teaching finding: outer/inner-only swap
+
+A lawful easy lesson assembled from seed `2`, demonstration sample indices
+`0, 1, 2`, and query sample index `3` has ring counts `3, 2, 2, 4` and dimensions
+`6×8, 8×4, 4×6, 8×8`. The plausible rival “exchange only the outermost and
+innermost colors, leaving other rings fixed” matches all three demonstrations
+and disagrees on the query. Its input ring colors are `[4, 2, 7, 5]`; the
+canonical answer has `[5, 7, 2, 4]`, while the rival has `[5, 2, 7, 4]`.
+
+`workspace/review_learnability.py` replays the complete canonical and rival
